{#
    The mark in the bar.

    What it says is configuration, not a template a project has to copy. In its
    `guides.xml`:

        <extension class="TYPO3\Soul\GuidesTheme\DependencyInjection\SoulExtension">
            <signet>_images/signet.svg</signet>
            <brand>Acme</brand>
            <product>Your product</product>
        </extension>

    All three are optional. With no product the bar carries the project title
    from `<project>`, which is where a name belongs when there is only one.

    The pipe is drawn by the stylesheet — a 2px accent rule, and one of exactly
    three places that colour appears — so it is written as an empty span and
    never as a `|`. It appears only where there are two halves to separate: a
    single name is the mark itself, in the mark's own weight, rather than the
    quiet half of a lockup with nothing beside it.

    The version is not in here. It is a badge at the other end of the bar, with
    the rest of what is true of the page rather than of the product, and it goes
    with them when the bar narrows.

    The signet path is relative to the documentation root and must be a file
    the renderer can see — beside the documents, so it is copied into the
    output with them rather than pointing at something that exists only on the
    machine that built the site.

    A signet is NOT an icon: it ships at three optical sizes with different
    construction, and bar height is the small one's job.
#}
<a class="sds-lockup" href="{{ soul.home ? asset(soul.home) : renderLink('/index') }}">
    {%- if soul.signet %}
        <img class="sds-signet" src="{{ asset('/' ~ soul.signet) }}" alt="" width="24" height="24" />
    {%- endif %}
    {%- set name = soul.product|default(env.projectNode.title)|default('Documentation') %}
    <span class="sds-wordmark">
        {%- if soul.brand -%}
            {{ soul.brand }}<span class="sds-wordmark__pipe" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sds-wordmark__product">{{ name }}</span>
        {%- else -%}
            {{ name }}
        {%- endif -%}
    </span>
</a>
